# Cline Project Rules — SmartGrid Landing Page

> Cline's operating instructions for the SmartGrid repo. For the canonical team coding
> standards and full project context, also read `AGENTS.md` in the repo root.

## Project at a Glance
- Next.js 16 **Pages Router** + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4, `src/`-layout.
- i18n via `next-i18next` (locales: `en, de, sw, fr, pt`). Custom hook: `src/hooks/useTranslation.ts`.
- Content from Sanity CMS + `public/locales/*/....json` files. Product registry in `products.json`.
- Five locales must be kept in sync on every change (text translated, URLs/slugs/codes copied verbatim).

## How Cline Should Operate
- **Never fabricate.** If something is ambiguous (missing context, unclear intent), ask the user
  with a concrete, specific question before acting.
- **Find the real file.** Pages live in `src/pages/[locale]/...`; the root `src/pages/*.tsx` files
  are thin re-export proxies — edit the `[locale]` source, not the proxy. Components live in
  `src/components/...`; layouts in `src/layouts/LandingPage/`.
- **Validate with the toolchain.** After making changes run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`,
  then `npm run build`. Do not consider a task complete until these pass.
- **Mind the dev server.** Before starting one, check whether a server is already running on
  port 3000. Start one only for manual verification, then stop/terminate it. Never leave it running.
- **Never commit secrets.** `.env.local` is gitignored. Only `.env.example` is versioned.
- **i18n discipline.** Any edit to a locale JSON must be applied to every locale that has a
  corresponding file. Text → translate; URLs/slugs/hrefs/codes → copy verbatim.

## Coding Standards (must follow)
- Functional components with **explicit return types** (`function X(): ReactElement`).
- **Tabs (size 4)**, double quotes, es5 trailing commas, 100-column print width
  (Prettier + EditorConfig — do not fight the formatter).
- **Semantic HTML** — no generic `<div>` where a `<section>` / `<nav>` / `<header>` fits.
- **Performance first** — `dynamic(..., { ssr: false })` for Three.js / GSAP / heavy
  animations; `priority` + `fetchPriority="high"` on the LCP hero image; lazy-load images.
- **No unused imports** (`eslint-plugin-unused-imports` is an error).
- Use the **`@/*`** alias (→ `./src/*`); import `useTranslation` from `@/hooks`; use
  `@/components/Link` and `<PageHead pageName="..." />`.

## Commands Cline Should Know
| Command            | What it does                                |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |
| `npm run dev`      | Dev server on http://localhost:3000         |
| `npm run build`    | Production build + `next-sitemap` postbuild |
| `npm run lint`     | ESLint (fails on any warning)               |
| `npm run lint:fix` | Auto-fix lint issues                        |
| `npm run typecheck`| `tsc --noEmit`                              |
| `npm run typegen`  | Sanity schema extract + typegen             |

## Constraints / Guardrails
- Do not modify `AGENTS.md`, `.clinerules`, `CLAUDE.md`, or `README.md` unless explicitly asked.
- Respect existing design tokens in `src/styles/globals.css` (primary `#0097b2`, accent `#975604`).
- Do not change locale URLs/slugs without mirroring the exact value across all locales.
- Stay within the confirmed tech stack (Next.js 16, Tailwind v4, React 19, Sanity, Zustand,
  Zod, Framer Motion, GSAP, Lenis, Three.js, next-i18next). Do not pull in new libraries
  unless the user explicitly requests it.